      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Flint River borders the county’s west, its alluvial floodplain giving Lilly surrounding farmland its fertile soil.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lilly_georgia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lilly was formally incorporated in 1907, adopting a unique circular city limit that wrapped around surrounding agricultural land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lilly_georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1920 fire razed downtown, prompting a rebuild in brick and frame that showcases Greek Revival, Queen Anne, Folk Victorian, and Craftsman styles.",
